Everything would work offline because you control the entire blockchain.

3. Local Testnet
We can even create a local blockchain network where several computers on the same LAN participate.

One computer becomes the seed node.

Other computers connect to it.

No internet required—just the local network.

This is a great way to learn distributed systems.

4. Distributed Computing Platform
If the goal is to use spare CPU/GPU resources, another direction is a distributed computing application.

Instead of mining cryptocurrency, the machines could work together to solve useful problems, such as:

AI model training

image processing

video rendering

scientific simulations

This is often a more productive use of computing power than cryptocurrency mining.

